---
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';
import SiteLink from '../components/SiteLink.astro';
import { APP_NAME, BUSINESS_NAME, SUPPORT_EMAIL } from '../utils/env';

const effectiveDateISO = '2026-09-17';
const effectiveDateLabel = 'September 17, 2026';
---

<Doc
  title="Privacy"
  description={`How ${APP_NAME} handles your data and what you can do about it.`}
>
  <header class="doc__header">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
  </header>

  <p>{APP_NAME} is published by {BUSINESS_NAME}.</p>

  <section>
    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      {APP_NAME} sends stats to <SiteLink href="https://telemetrydeck.com/privacy/" target="_blank" aria-label="TelemetryDeck privacy policy, opens in new tab">TelemetryDeck</SiteLink> only if you say yes when the app
      first asks. Those stats cover how you use the app and the purchases you
      make, along with crashes, errors and performance. They also include app
      and device details such as your device model, OS version, region and
      language, and each install sends its own random ID with them.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can change your answer in the app's settings, and turning stats off
      stops anything more from being sent. Anything that's already been sent
      is kept with no set deletion date. Because it isn't tied to your name,
      email or Apple Account, we can't pick out your past records to delete
      them. Reset Data in the app gives this install a new random ID.
    </p>
    <p>
      TelemetryDeck has to protect that data the way this policy and Apple's
      privacy rules require.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Your data</h2>
    <p>
      If you want to delete the game's data, open Settings in the game and go
      to Privacy. Reset Data (This Device) clears this device, while Reset
      Across All Devices also clears iCloud, so each of your other devices
      clears the next time you open the game on it. Either reset gives that
      device a new analytics
      ID, but it doesn't delete analytics we've already received, and it
      never touches your purchases.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Content reports</h2>
    <p>
      Content reports go out by email from your own mail account, so a report
      carries your email address. Each one includes the reason you type,
      along with the round ID, the word pack, how many guesses were made, and
      the app version and build. Once the word has been revealed, the report
      includes it too. The drawing is attached only if you say yes when the
      app asks, and you're free to send the report without it. We use reports
      to review what was reported.
    </p>
    <p>
      We keep report emails in the support inbox, and if you'd like one deleted, email <SiteLink href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</SiteLink> from the address that sent it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Tracking</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing in {APP_NAME} tracks activity in other apps or on websites.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We'll post important changes to this policy here.</p>
  </section>

  <footer class="doc__meta">Effective <time datetime={effectiveDateISO}>{effectiveDateLabel}</time>.</footer>
</Doc>
